      "narration": "So why does Alaska pay you to live there? Because in nineteen seventy-six, it decided that oil money belonged to everyone, and locked it away. That fund grew to about ninety-two billion dollars. But once the state started paying its bills from the same account, every dividend became a choice. The check is not shrinking by accident. It is shrinking by vote. Every spring, the legislature decides again how much of the oil fortune goes to people, and how much goes to the government. The fund keeps growing. The argument over the check does too.",
